,"avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T21:57:11-07:00","id":878451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=877962#post877962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For you, maybe. But let's not go around stating it like a matter of fact, for some of us it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can appreciate and respect that some people enjoy 3e. In the same way, I can appreciate and respect that some people enjoy eating at, say, Applebee's. Enjoying a mediocre product however, does not stop it from being mediocre.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878173#post878173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get the &quot;not lived up to the hype&quot; complaint considering the 3E core delivers exactly what the writers said it would. If you don't like what they aimed to do that's a matter of taste not quality since it does successfully do the things they said they were aiming to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you're right. Maybe I'm holding the Devs to too high a standard.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to adhere to the standards they had set for themselves with their earlier work in 2.5e.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to write charms that are flavorful and evocative, that wow me as a player and fire my imagination, as opposed to simple dice tricks.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to write tight, clean and concise rules that ease the burden on the GM and facilitate ease of play.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to remove a problematic mechanic that has been known since the early days of 2e (Bonus Points) now that we have a whole new edition.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to, after almost 4 years, have examined the implications such charms as God-King's Shrike, Duel Magnus Prana, or Celestial Bliss Trick.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong. Who knows. I'm sure it's all subjective anyway, and that quality is just an empty word with no meaning.<br /> <br /> Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 04-30-2016, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:14:07-07:00","id":878461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878451#post878451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can appreciate and respect that some people enjoy 3e. In the same way, I can appreciate and respect that some people enjoy eating at, say, Applebee's. Enjoying a mediocre product however, does not stop it from being mediocre.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really not at all a fair comparison. That you don't care for it doesn't make it mediocre. The devs pretty clearly had a solid creative vision for this edition that they executed on. That makes them something very different than the Applebee's of TTRPGs. You don't have to like what they made, but come on, man. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to adhere to the standards they had set for themselves with their earlier work in 2.5e. </div> </div> </div>Okay, these are internal attributions that you have no way of knowing anything about. I cannot claim to say what standards they were using, but given what I have seen of John and Holden, I am inclined to believe it's pretty high. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to write charms that are flavorful and evocative, that wow me as a player and fire my imagination, as opposed to simple dice tricks. </div> </div> </div>Taste again, but I vehemently disagree. I think the broad spread of the charms are cool and evocative, and that in my play experience these tricks enhance feel of play at my table. May not be for you, again, taste is subjective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong for expecting them to, after almost 4 years, have examined the implications such charms as God-King's Shrike, Duel Magnus Prana, or Celestial Bliss Trick. </div> </div> </div>You mean powers where the essential problem comes down to table-level conduct which amounts to don't be a dick with the powers at your disposal in a game where one of the guiding principles explicitly spelled out in the rules is pretty much don't be a destructive dick?<br /> <br /> I can understand that people have frustrations with the game, the system and the devs. I can see how the language of the book, the tone that is presented in places, the spread of charms and their mechanics can frustrate people. That some people take issue with something does not make it of lessened quality. I am also, quite frankly tired of people uncharitibly interpreting both the rules text and the words of the devs at every turn. I'm not specifically accusing you of this, JayTee, but I see it happen a lot and it pushes me away from the community. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:21:17-07:00","id":878464,"title":"","content":"Powerful and balanced can and do live together, especially in the Solar Charm set. Trust me, I'm a doctor!<br /> <br /> (Writing the Medicine tree is kind of like being a doctor, right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":25}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:22:24-07:00","id":878466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878464#post878464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Writing the Medicine tree is kind of like being a doctor, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Close enough for government work.<br /> <br /> (makes Bureaucracy check)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:23:05-07:00","id":878467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878451#post878451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T22:31:15-07:00","id":878473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878461#post878461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really not at all a fair comparison. That you don't care for it doesn't make it mediocre. The devs pretty clearly had a solid creative vision for this edition that they executed on. That makes them something very different than the Applebee's of TTRPGs. You don't have to like what they made, but come on, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was expecting Gordon Ramsy, and instead I got Chef Joe. How else was I supposed to feel about all this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878461#post878461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, these are internal attributions that you have no way of knowing anything about. I cannot claim to say what standards they were using, but given what I have seen of John and Holden, I am inclined to believe it's pretty high.<br /> <br /> Taste again, but I vehemently disagree. I think the broad spread of the charms are cool and evocative, and that in my play experience these tricks enhance feel of play at my table. May not be for you, again, taste is subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 2e, they were working within the bounds of a broken system and still managed to produce content that was flavorful and engaging, and helped me get through a lot of the mechanical slog of 2e because of how amazing it was. With the opportunity to write the bounds of the new system, I expected this to continue. It didn't. Instead they <i>contributed </i>to the mechanical slog<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878461#post878461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean powers where the essential problem comes down to table-level conduct which amounts to don't be a dick with the powers at your disposal in a game where one of the guiding principles explicitly spelled out in the rules is pretty much don't be a destructive dick?</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect (and I mean that genuinely as opposed to sarcastically) I believe you are making the <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Oberoni_Fallacy\" target=\"_blank\">Oberoni Fallacy</a>, so you'll have to forgive me if I... dismiss? (there needs to be a nicer word for that) this claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878461#post878461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand that people have frustrations with the game, the system and the devs. I can see how the language of the book, the tone that is presented in places, the spread of charms and their mechanics can frustrate people. That some people take issue with something does not make it of lessened quality. I am also, quite frankly tired of people uncharitibly interpreting both the rules text and the words of the devs at every turn. I'm not specifically accusing you of this, JayTee, but I see it happen a lot and it pushes me away from the community.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, props and respect for keeping this impersonal with your last sentence. Better than I did with Molez and Glamourweaver (My bad to each of you, I got cross and let it get the best of me).<br /> <br /> More on point, sadly there isn't much room for interpretation. The text of the charms are right there in the book. Much of it is unclear, which in turn hurts speed of play, which in turn make the game less ideal than it could have been. I'm not asking for perfection, but I am asking for a level of quality that I have been given previously. I don't think this is unreasonable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:11:12-07:00","id":878517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878473#post878473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting Gordon Ramsy, and instead I got Chef Joe. How else was I supposed to feel about all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Agree to disagree. Clearly we're not gonna see eye-to-eye, but I think that your framing is actively insulting to years of hard work on the part of the developers and writers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With 2e, they were working within the bounds of a broken system and still managed to produce content that was flavorful and engaging, and helped me get through a lot of the mechanical slog of 2e because of how amazing it was. With the opportunity to write the bounds of the new system, I expected this to continue. It didn't. Instead they <i>contributed </i>to the mechanical slog </div> </div> </div>Again, different strokes. My play experiences have been pretty smooth and breezy so far with a few different groups. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With all due respect (and I mean that genuinely as opposed to sarcastically) I believe you are making the <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Oberoni_Fallacy\" target=\"_blank\">Oberoni Fallacy</a>, so you'll have to forgive me if I... dismiss? (there needs to be a nicer word for that) this claim. </div> </div> </div>This is fair. I'm not sure how best to navigate rule zero in the light of the golden and orichalcum rules, but their presence in the system seems to indicate to me that the potential for people to abuse mechanics, thereby breaking social and narrative contract are in the domain of individual tables and are no reason not to include cool, flavorful powers at the high end of play. I'll accept that this is, though textually supported, fallacious reasoning, even if that reasoning appears to be shared by developers. Writing that I absolutely realize that that has every reason to upset you! You are definitely entitled to that upset. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First off, props and respect for keeping this impersonal with your last sentence. Better than I did with Molez and Glamourweaver (My bad to each of you, I got cross and let it get the best of me).<br /> <br /> More on point, sadly there isn't much room for interpretation. The text of the charms are right there in the book. Much of it is unclear, which in turn hurts speed of play, which in turn make the game less ideal than it could have been. I'm not asking for perfection, but I am asking for a level of quality that I have been given previously. I don't think this is unreasonable. </div> </div> </div>Again, I haven't been dealing with a lot of clarity issues at my table and in play. I know there are some weird potential interactions in the rules (esp. around counterattacks) and I recognize the validity of those. I have also seen some people being very uncheritable or deliberately obtuse (I recall some very strange interpretations of archery charms such as to make them useless). I'm not saying the system is above criticism or without issue. My experience is that this is not as endemic as some make it out to be. This could be table-level stuff where the people in the games I am playing in are like to interpret rules in the same way that I do. I don't know. I can only really say that it has yet to be a major issue or impediment to the flow of my own games. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:12:35-07:00","id":878518,"title":"","content":"It's going to be like this whenever John posts, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Forever more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:32:47-07:00","id":878530,"title":"","content":"Sadly, yes it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:48:14-07:00","id":878542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878517#post878517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Agree to disagree. Clearly we're not gonna see eye-to-eye, but I think that your framing is actively insulting to years of hard work on the part of the developers and writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less an insult and more an expression of incredible disappointment. I know they can produce way way way better content than this, but for some reason, they... didn't. It's like listening to a band produce great music despite being given shitty instruments (2e), and then when they have the chance to custom-desgin their own instruments from scratch (3e) the music suddenly goes from fantastic to bafflingly average, and you're stuck wondering what the hell happened to all that great stuff they produced.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878517#post878517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is fair. I'm not sure how best to navigate rule zero in the light of the golden and orichalcum rules, but their presence in the system seems to indicate to me that the potential for people to abuse mechanics, thereby breaking social and narrative contract are in the domain of individual tables and are no reason not to include cool, flavorful powers at the high end of play. I'll accept that this is, though textually supported, fallacious reasoning, even if that reasoning appears to be shared by developers. Writing that I absolutely realize that that has every reason to upset you! You are definitely entitled to that upset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I uh... can't tell if you're being sarcastic or not with that last bit. In the interest of keeping this civil, I'll assume you're not being sarcastic, though. I'm not really all that upset by the rule zero fallacy, just pointing out that it's not really all that great of an argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878517#post878517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I haven't been dealing with a lot of clarity issues at my table and in play. I know there are some weird potential interactions in the rules (esp. around counterattacks) and I recognize the validity of those. I have also seen some people being very uncheritable or deliberately obtuse (I recall some very strange interpretations of archery charms such as to make them useless). I'm not saying the system is above criticism or without issue. My experience is that this is not as endemic as some make it out to be. This could be table-level stuff where the people in the games I am playing in are like to interpret rules in the same way that I do. I don't know. I can only really say that it has yet to be a major issue or impediment to the flow of my own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the real deciding factor on the clarity of the rules/charms will be later on, when/if we get dozens of threads all asking for clarification on the same issues over and over, or discussing what the intended purpose of XYZ is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 04-30-2016, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:57:10-07:00","id":878546,"title":"","content":"On Rule Zero, my take is those Charms are better there than not. Because I think that interesting, genre-emulating effects like thsoe are more important to have than not. But I also am of the opnion that it's not possible to get something everyone always likes, so I err on the side of being able to provid emore options than to restrict things on the basis that some people are assholes.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:39:51-07:00","id":878569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878464#post878464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Trust me, I'm <b>The D</b>octor! ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:50:07-07:00","id":878575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878542#post878542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less an insult and more an expression of incredible disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you insult someone without meaning to, that doesn't change whether or not it <i>is</i> an insult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:56:24-07:00","id":878579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878466#post878466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Close enough for government work.<br /> <br /> (makes Bureaucracy check)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The reason this is funny to me is I knew and worked with a guy for a time who said that. Also said things like &quot;I might wear gloves when working with this contact neruotoxin if it were a <b>cumulative neurotoxin</b>. But it's not.&quot; Pretty sloppy in some ways, but got things to always work out.<br /> <br /> On Exalted living up to the hype, it didn't (based on my thoughts). Before you burn me in effigy, bear with me here. A) Hype often is started with a seed planted by the makers, but doesn't always have much added after that. There's a reason they call it the Hype Train. A lot of the hype was created by fans, not the devs. B) As such, things that people are going to care the most about tend to get the most hype. Exalted I think we can count there. C) As such expectations can get so high that a game could be great and still not live up to the hype. Exalted would have had to have been the One Core, the book to rule them all and in shininess bind them. I've played video games for years, and the Hype Train is a terrible creature.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, Exalted doesn't live up to the hype, but it'd pretty much have to turn <b>YOU </b>into an Exalt to live up to the hype expectations. As such, I think it can both be true it didn't live up to the hype and that it's a pretty good to very good game (depending on player/ST).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:59:39-07:00","id":878584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878575#post878575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you insult someone without meaning to, that doesn't change whether or not it <i>is</i> an insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone takes a statement of disappointment as an insult, then I, unfortunately, really can't help that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:13:10-07:00","id":878589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=876768#post876768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted's Earth-based fans died as they lived - in a massive round of flaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>saw this and for some reason I have to say the following, &quot;I live, I die, I play Exalted again.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:26:59-07:00","id":878598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878579#post878579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In conclusion, Exalted doesn't live up to the hype, but it'd pretty much have to turn <b>YOU </b>into an Exalt to live up to the hype expectations. As such, I think it can both be true it didn't live up to the hype and that it's a pretty good to very good game (depending on player/ST).</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Perhaps a better question is &quot;Are you happy with the product you got?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I certainly am, my grumbles aside. It's STILL one of the best systems I've played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:41:43-07:00","id":878605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878598#post878598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Perhaps a better question is &quot;Are you happy with the product you got?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I certainly am, my grumbles aside. It's STILL one of the best systems I've played.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure on best I've played, but I'm very happy with the product. And on the &quot;best I've played&quot;, it's more I need more time to think about it. I won't lie, sometimes I find stuff like combat very hard to keep all in mind (but that likely has a lot to do with how little combat we've had in the game I'm in). I'm EXTREMELY happy with the charms, and any charms I've made are more specialty stuff that fits my character (with the understanding that I got ST ok after they looked them over). Quite a bit to love. I think I'm where you are for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T04:19:24-07:00","id":878654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less an insult and more an expression of incredible disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div> An expression of diappointment that framed the subject in bad terms. &quot;Oh, I'm disappointed by how much you suck. Hey, don't be <b>insulted</b> or anything, I'm just expressing how you sucking so much made me feel!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T06:12:11-07:00","id":878688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878542#post878542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I uh... can't tell if you're being sarcastic or not with that last bit. In the interest of keeping this civil, I'll assume you're not being sarcastic, though. I'm not really all that upset by the rule zero fallacy, just pointing out that it's not really all that great of an argument.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not being sarcastic. I recognize that it isn't a great argument. I'm not trying to construct an excellent argument as much as I am trying to construct an explanatory framework for why things might be the way they are, which advances from developer intent. Intent, which as far as I have seen explained, I agree with. I am also trying to understand how and why the game might not sit well with people. It's about why things might be the way they are and not in the logical defense of why that may or may not be. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T07:49:01-07:00","id":878719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878654#post878654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An expression of diappointment that framed the subject in bad terms. &quot;Oh, I'm disappointed by how much you suck. Hey, don't be <b>insulted</b> or anything, I'm just expressing how you sucking so much made me feel!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll stop using the metaphor when it stops being appropriate. Applebee's isn't bad, it's just not Restaurant Gordon Ramsay. When Gordon Ramsay serves you Applebee's, you're inclined to ask what the heck happened with no small amount of incredulity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monkipi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878688#post878688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not being sarcastic. I recognize that it isn't a great argument. I'm not trying to construct an excellent argument as much as I am trying to construct an explanatory framework for why things might be the way they are, which advances from developer intent. Intent, which as far as I have seen explained, I agree with. I am also trying to understand how and why the game might not sit well with people. It's about why things might be the way they are and not in the logical defense of why that may or may not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's the crux of the whole issue, in that 3e seems to be heavily dependent on rule zero for interpretation. It's like an upside-down pyramid resting on it's point, and needs constant checking and readjustment to make sure it doesn't get unbalanced and fall over. Some people like that, and that's fine. Personally, I prefer a pyramid that's balanced on it's base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T07:51:35-07:00","id":878720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878719#post878719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll stop using the metaphor when it stops being appropriate. Applebee's isn't bad, it's just not Restaurant Gordon Ramsay. When Gordon Ramsay serves you Applebee's, you're inclined to ask what the heck happened with no small amount of incredulity.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all respect due, I don't think the average layperson is gonna know the difference. Have you eaten at a celebrity chef's restaurant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:00:25-07:00","id":878729,"title":"","content":"Can we get some preview of those charms? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9120-akodo","name":"Akodo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:00:31-07:00","id":878730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll stop using the metaphor when it stops being appropriate. Applebee's isn't bad, it's just not Restaurant Gordon Ramsay. When Gordon Ramsay serves you Applebee's, you're inclined to ask what the heck happened with no small amount of incredulity.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;See, being insulting is okay when I decide it's okay, and it's not even really all that insulting anyway.&quot; You just keep on running for cover, there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:30:22-07:00","id":878751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878720#post878720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all respect due, I don't think the average layperson is gonna know the difference. Have you eaten at a celebrity chef's restaurant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once, it was a graduation present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878730#post878730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;See, being insulting is okay when I decide it's okay, and it's not even really all that insulting anyway.&quot; You just keep on running for cover, there.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you keep talking down to me as though your assessment is somehow magically more valid than mine, chief. I'm sure that'll show me the error of my ways.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is any more value to this conversation, so I'm going to withdraw before threadlock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 04-30-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:36:35-07:00","id":878756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878719#post878719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll stop using the metaphor when it stops being appropriate. Applebee's isn't bad, it's just not Restaurant Gordon Ramsay. When Gordon Ramsay serves you Applebee's, you're inclined to ask what the heck happened with no small amount of incredulity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of seems like you are a victim of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HypeBacklash\" target=\"_blank\">Hype Backlash</a> more than anything else.<br /> <br /> Part of selling any product or funding kickstarter means you need to generate interest so those fans can get others interested, so you can actually get the money funded to run the product.<br /> OPP are presumably on a shoestring budget, with Pugmire possibly being the first product they can run from internal funding rather than preorders and freelancer goodwill.<br /> <br /> At that level, you need Hype or the product never exists.<br /> <br /> I've backed many KSers and no matter what the product from <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1554093685/erfworld-motion-comic-project/comments\" target=\"_blank\">webcomic funding</a> to <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1650950769/rigidbot-3d-printer/comments\" target=\"_blank\">3d printing </a>to <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1523379957/oculus-rift-step-into-the-game/comments\" target=\"_blank\">VR</a>, Murphy's law always applies, and often the biggest fans experience the biggest backlash.<br /> Am I saying criticism is forbidden? No, but recognising the same pattern is there prevents you from getting overhyped and thus disillusioned, and to take a break from one experience, subscribe to the kickstarter RSS feed and do something else for a bit.<br /> <br /> In this case, the Backer PDF is in art layout! it's completely optional! it'll be cheap!<br /> <br /> Fast reasonable updates are exactly what we want now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:42:34-07:00","id":878760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>doran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878756#post878756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It kind of seems like you are a victim of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HypeBacklash\" target=\"_blank\">Hype Backlash</a> more than anything else.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be honest here. After years of waiting, even if God himself designed Exalted 3rd Edition to be the perfect RPG system, Ex3 would <b>never</b> live up to its hype. <br /> <br /> It's okay to be mad though. In hindsight, I'm glad I wasn't paying attention to Exalted when the Kickstarter ran. If I was a backer, I'd be long gone by now and moved on to other things. But since I didn't have money invested in the product and only waited for the game for a year and a half, here I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:45:40-07:00","id":878761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878760#post878760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's be honest here. After years of waiting, even if God himself designed Exalted 3rd Edition to be the perfect RPG system, Ex3 would <b>never</b> live up to its hype.<br /> <br /> It's okay to be mad though. In hindsight, I'm glad I wasn't paying attention to Exalted when the Kickstarter ran. If I was a backer, I'd be long gone by now and moved on to other things. But since I didn't have money invested in the product and only waited for the game for a year and a half, here I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just dealt with by focusing on other stuff, joined a Dresden files game, played some online Genius The Transgression, currently playing Shadowrun as a player and working out a plan to run Ex3. Waiting is just something the more you think about the worse it gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:53:31-07:00","id":878767,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit lost as to where all the hype is coming from that got people's expectations so unrealistically high. Like, OK, some of the promotional material and developer comments, particularly early on, were to the effect of &quot;this will be the best game ever and everything will be fantastic&quot; but that's pretty much par for the course for &quot;thing a developer says about a product currently in development&quot;. 3e's certainly flawed in some unfortunate ways, like any other game, but in most respects it exceeded my expectations appreciably, and my expectations would probably have been <i>lower </i>if I'd taken the forum scuttlebutt to heart. I mean, JayTee, I don't really remember you posting a lot about how excited you were and how great 3e was going to be before it came out, which is kind of what I'd expect if you were fooled by hype?<br /> <br /> It's good; it's probably the best high-crunch RPG I've seen, and easily the best one working under Exalted's design constraints. It is, in fact, appreciably better balanced and playtested than the average OPP product. I feel like the game has too many charms and I'm <i>still</i> enthusiastic about the backer charm PDF adding more, because so many of them are so rad. On the other hand, in the early phase people were free to imagine it being anything they wanted out of Exalted since details were scant, and now that it's a specific thing, a lot of those people find that it's not (or not exactly) the thing they want. I think that's more attributable to the sense of disappointment some people seem to be feeling than &quot;hype&quot; -- the attitude that, &quot;well, given all this time and work, why <i>didn't</i> they make the game the way I'd have wanted it to be made?&quot; But given that there have always been a thousand competing visions for Exalted, it didn't take much perspicacity to realize in advance that that wasn't likely to happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T09:11:36-07:00","id":878783,"title":"","content":"I do kind of think the KS was maybe a bit early. It shows with a few of other OPP's gamelines, as a note. WIth how they were being talked about, I expected <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken 2e </b>in 2013 or early 2014 as well, not mid-2015. And we're also still waiting on <b>Mage: the Awakening 2e</b>. Scion and Trinity to me felt like they were ready to be out in 2014, but we have barely got some preview stuff and Scion's corebook smoving into the first draft.<br /> <br /> I think that a big issue on Exalted's delay being so frustrating is that it was KS'd before we knew what OPP's real pipeline capability was.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T10:01:18-07:00","id":878829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/876347-exalted-returns-the-solar-backer-charm-pdf?p=878783#post878783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we're also still waiting on Mage: the Awakening 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> For four more days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T10:40:02-07:00","id":878856,"title":"","content":"Because one &quot;I am mad&quot; thread wasn't enough to contain people... <b>I'm no mod</b>, but I would comfortably say the subject has veered off the OP. If you don't like the idea of the backer charms, that's legit. If you're complaining about what the base game didn't deliver, there are already threads for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 04-30-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T10:53:09-07:00","id":878867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quot